// surface_lambda.tk -- lambda, local named function, `use (a, &b)` (K4, D221
// §41): the explicit form `new Op((T a, T b) => body)`, over the same
// object K1's plain-function wrap already builds. K4b adds a delegate
// captured BY VALUE (item 11) and the contextual/short grafias (items 12/13).
// K4c adds a clean `f` unrelated to `byref_check`'s own (item 14) and a
// ternary of two function names coerced into a delegate (item 15).
//
// What each helper proves, in order:
//
//   1. `nocap_check` -- a lambda with no capture at all.
//   2. `byval_check` -- `use (k)` freezes a COPY at construction: mutating
//      the declarer's `k` afterward does not change what the closure reads.
//   3. `byref_check` -- `use (&acc)` derefs the declarer's OWN slot, and a
//      second call sees what the first one left there.
//   4. `two_lambdas_check` -- two closures of the SAME delegate type, each
//      with its own capture, do not step on one another.
//   5. `local_named_check` -- `Op twice = new Op(...)`, D221 decision 22's
//      own reading of a "local named function".
//   6. `method_check` -- a lambda stored in a field and called through
//      `this.cb(x)`, one passed as a METHOD argument (explicit AND
//      contextual grafia) and called there.
//   7. `counted_check` -- `use (b)` of a class reference: the closure holds
//      its own count, `rt_live()` stays at 1 after the declarer's own `b`
//      is dropped, and drops to 0 only once the closure itself is released.
//   8. `geo.use_lambda()` -- the same machinery inside a `namespace`.
//   9. `block_check` -- a lambda with a BLOCK body, `=> { ...; return e; }`.
//  10. `free_arg_check` -- `new Op(...)` as the argument of a FREE function.
//  11. `deleg_byval_check` -- a delegate itself captured BY VALUE (K4b).
//  12. `contextual_check` -- `Op f = (i64 x) use (k) => x * k;`, no `new`.
//  13. `short_check` -- `Op g = x => x + 1;`, the single-parameter grafia.
//  14. `clean_f_returns_check` -- a CLEAN `f`, in a function of its own,
//      returned as-is: `byref_check`'s own `f` captures by reference and
//      must not taint this one just because the two share a name (K4c).
//  15. `ternary_check` -- `flag ? add1 : double_it` coerced into `Op`, both
//      as a `return` and as a plain initializer (K4c).
//  16. `global_const_free_check` -- a lambda with NO `use (...)` at all reads
//      a global (live, not frozen), reads a `const`, calls a free function
//      and WRITES the global back, all visible to the caller afterward
//      (D226 compat crumb item 3).
//  17. `nested_check` (higiene 2, item 6) -- a lambda literal built INSIDE
//      another one's own body, `use (k)` at BOTH levels: the shared capture
//      table used to reset to 0 at either end of the INNER lambda's own
//      `tk_lambda_finish`, wiping out the OUTER's still-in-progress capture
//      of the same name (`k`) and refusing it as "not captured" once the
//      outer's own body walk ran.
//  18. `manycap_check` (higiene 3, item B) -- FIFTEEN captures in one
//      `use (...)`, fourteen by value and one by reference. The allocator
//      used to take one PARAMETER per capture, so anything past twelve died
//      on the mc ABI's own `at most 12 parameters`; it now takes the object
//      and the captures are written at the creation site.
//  19. `midbody_gen_check` (K6) -- a construct that GENERATES a top-level
//      declaration mid-body, written BEFORE a lambda that captures by
//      reference: an explicit thunk (`new Op(add1)`), the three declarations
//      `new i64[n]` needs, and a generic instance. `top_add` clears
//      `p_decl_name()`, so each of them used to leave the rest of the body
//      with no owner at all, and the `use (&acc)` below then keyed its escape
//      under a null one -- a segmentation fault inside the compiler, at the
//      `str_eq` of `tk_taint_find` (teko_deleg.tk). Written in the natural
//      order, it now compiles, and `made` and the closure both answer.
//  20. `partial_close_check` (K6) -- the same trap from the other side: a
//      `partial class` closes at its first USE, so a `new Shape()` in the
//      middle of a body is what emits the vtable, the interface table, the
//      release and the allocators. Those were the last generators still
//      adding through a bare `top_add`, and a `use (&acc)` written after the
//      `new` crashed the compiler exactly as item 19 did.
//  21. `accessor_owner_check` (K6) -- an ARROW accessor (`get => ...;` /
//      `set => ...;`) reads its own body instead of handing it to
//      `parse_function`, so it used to belong to no declaration at all: once
//      any lambda above had tainted a name, the `set`'s own statement asked
//      `tk_taint_owner` and got a null owner -- the same crash, without a
//      single generated declaration involved.
//  22. `slot_roads_check` (D66) -- a contextual lambda written straight into
//      every slot of delegate type the language has a parse position for: an
//      instance FIELD (`h.cb = (i64 x) => x + 1;`, both grafias and a capture
//      by value), a STATIC field (`St.cb = ...`), `this.cb = ...` inside a
//      constructor, and an `Op[]` ELEMENT. Each of them died in mc's own
//      parser, `expected ) in cast`, and each had to be written
//      `new Op((i64 x) => ...)` instead; `method_check` above, which did
//      exactly that, is written the direct way now.
//  23. `arg_roads_check` (D66, Copilot on #719) -- the three METHOD-argument
//      shapes the first reader missed, because it asked the callee's single
//      declaration for the parameter's type: a parameter declared `Op?`, an
//      OVERLOADED name (which signature applies is not known until the
//      argument COUNT is, but every candidate spells the same delegate at
//      that position), and a method INHERITED from a base, whose name the
//      derived class itself declares zero times. A GROUP at a delegate
//      argument and a CAST at the position beside it measure the other half:
//      the lookahead claims neither.
//  24. `member_check` (D70) -- a lambda judged against the ENCLOSING CLASS's
//      own members before any global of the identical name ever gets a
//      look: a STATIC field, a member CONST and a STATIC property, each
//      read bare, with a same-named global standing right beside the class
//      to prove the member -- not the global -- wins.
//  25. `member_deleg_check` (D70) -- the fourth member shape, kept apart
//      from item 24: a STATIC field of DELEGATE type, called bare inside a
//      lambda a STATIC method builds. Its own slot outlives this function's
//      scope exactly as `St.cb` (item 22) does, so it runs beside
//      `slot_roads_check`, LAST, rather than beside the other three.
//
// expect-exit: 42

#include "../lib/rt.tk"

delegate i64 Op(i64 a);

i64 apply(Op f, i64 x) {
    return f(x);
}

i64 add1(i64 x) {
    return x + 1;
}

i64 double_it(i64 x) {
    return x * 2;
}

class Holder {
    public Op cb;

    public i64 run(i64 x) {
        return this.cb(x);
    }

    public i64 relay(Op f, i64 x) {
        return f(x);
    }
}

i64 boxes_released = 0;

class Box {
    public i64 v;

    public Box(i64 x) {
        v = x;
    }

    ~Box() {
        boxes_released = boxes_released + 1;
    }
}

delegate i64 BoxOp();

i64 glob_counter = 0;

const i64 STEP = 5;

i64 bump_free(i64 x) {
    return x + 1;
}

class Cell<T> {
    public T v;
}

interface Tagged {
    i64 tag();
}

partial class Shape : Tagged {
    public i64 w;
}

partial class Shape {
    public i64 h;

    public i64 tag() {
        return 7;
    }

    public i64 area() {
        return w * h;
    }
}

namespace geo {
    i64 use_lambda() {
        i64 k = 3;
        Op f = new Op((i64 x) use (k) => x * k);
        return f(5);
    }
}

// D70: a lambda judged against the ENCLOSING CLASS's own members before any
// global gets a look -- `member_check` below is the positive twin of
// `tests/refuse/lambda_field_name.tk`, `lambda_deleg_field_call.tk`,
// `lambda_prop_name.tk` and `lambda_method_name.tk`. Every global below
// SHARES a static member's own name, on purpose: the member has to win even
// when a global of the identical spelling stands ready to answer instead.
i64 d70_glob = 9;                     // no member of `D70Member` shares this name
i64 sfield = 111;                     // collides with `D70Member`'s own static FIELD
i64 SCONST = 222;                     // collides with `D70Member`'s own member CONST
i64 SProp  = 333;                     // collides with `D70Member`'s own static PROPERTY
i64 scb    = 444;                     // collides with `D70Member`'s own static delegate FIELD

class D70Member {
    public static i64 sfield;
    public const i64 SCONST = 4;
    public static i64 SProp { get; set; }
    public static Op scb;                 // D70: a STATIC delegate field -- its own
                                           // slot outlives every scope, exactly as
                                           // `St.cb` (slot_roads_check) already does
    public Op cb;

    public static i64 stwice(i64 x) {
        return x * 2;
    }

    public void armGlobal() {
        this.cb = new Op((i64 x) => x + d70_glob);
    }

    public void armStatic() {
        this.cb = new Op((i64 x) => x + sfield + stwice(x));
    }

    public void armConstProp() {
        this.cb = new Op((i64 x) => x + SCONST + SProp);
    }

    // D70: the STATIC delegate field above, called bare inside a lambda a
    // STATIC method builds -- it needs no receiver, exactly as the field's
    // own qualified spelling (`D70Member.scb(x)`) needs none. The result is
    // handed back through a LOCAL, not a second static slot, so only `scb`
    // itself -- not this closure too -- adds to the floor `rt_live()` never
    // drops below again.
    public static Op sarmDeleg() {
        return new Op((i64 x) => x + scb(x));
    }
}

i64 nocap_check() {
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) => x * 2);
    if (f(21) != 42) return 1;
    return 0;
}

i64 byval_check() {
    i64 k = 3;
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) use (k) => x * k);
    k = 999;
    if (f(5) != 15) return 1;
    return 0;
}

i64 byref_check() {
    i64 acc = 0;
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) use (&acc) => { acc = acc + x; return acc; });
    if (f(3) != 3) return 1;
    if (f(4) != 7) return 2;
    if (acc != 7) return 3;
    return 0;
}

i64 two_lambdas_check() {
    i64 k1 = 2;
    i64 k2 = 10;
    Op f1 = new Op((i64 x) use (k1) => x * k1);
    Op f2 = new Op((i64 x) use (k2) => x * k2);
    if (f1(5) != 10) return 1;
    if (f2(5) != 50) return 2;
    return 0;
}

i64 local_named_check() {
    Op twice = new Op((i64 x) => x * 2);
    if (twice(21) != 42) return 1;
    return 0;
}

i64 method_check() {
    Holder h = new Holder;
    h.cb = (i64 x) => x + 1;                                   // D66: no `new` on the field road
    if (h.run(41) != 42) return 1;
    if (h.relay(new Op((i64 x) => x - 1), 43) != 42) return 2;
    if (h.relay((i64 x) => x - 1, 43) != 42) return 3;         // contextual, no `new` (K4b)
    return 0;
}

i64 counted_check() {
    {
        BoxOp f;
        {
            Box b = new Box(9);
            f = new BoxOp(() use (b) => b.v);
            if (f() != 9) return 1;
        }                                          // the Box's own slot closes here
        if (rt_live() != 2) return 2;              // the closure keeps the Box alive
    }                                              // ...and the closure's closes here
    if (boxes_released != 1) return 3;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 4;
    return 0;
}

i64 block_check() {
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) => { i64 y = x * 2; return y + 1; });
    if (f(10) != 21) return 1;
    return 0;
}

i64 free_arg_check() {
    if (apply(new Op((i64 x) => x - 1), 43) != 42) return 1;
    return 0;
}

i64 deleg_byval_check() {
    Op inner = new Op((i64 x) => x + 1);
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) use (inner) => inner(x) * 2);
    if (f(4) != 10) return 1;
    return 0;
}

i64 contextual_check() {
    i64 k = 3;
    Op f = (i64 x) use (k) => x * k;
    if (f(5) != 15) return 1;
    return 0;
}

i64 short_check() {
    Op g = x => x + 1;
    if (g(41) != 42) return 1;
    return 0;
}

Op clean_f_returns() {
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) => x * 2);
    return f;
}

i64 clean_f_returns_check() {
    Op g = clean_f_returns();
    if (g(21) != 42) return 1;
    return 0;
}

Op ternary_pick(i64 flag) {
    return flag != 0 ? add1 : double_it;
}

i64 ternary_check() {
    Op p = ternary_pick(1);
    if (p(21) != 22) return 1;
    Op q = ternary_pick(0);
    if (q(21) != 42) return 2;
    i64 flag = 1;
    Op g = flag != 0 ? add1 : double_it;
    if (g(21) != 22) return 3;
    flag = 0;
    Op h = flag != 0 ? add1 : double_it;
    if (h(21) != 42) return 4;
    return 0;
}

i64 global_const_free_check() {
    glob_counter = 10;
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) => bump_free(x) + STEP + glob_counter);
    if (f(0) != 16) return 1;                      // bump_free(0)=1, STEP=5, glob_counter=10
    glob_counter = 20;
    if (f(0) != 26) return 2;                      // reads the LIVE global, not a frozen copy
    Op inc = new Op((i64 x) => { glob_counter = glob_counter + x; return glob_counter; });
    if (inc(5) != 25) return 3;                    // writes the global from inside the lambda
    if (glob_counter != 25) return 4;               // ...and the write reaches the real global
    return 0;
}

i64 nested_check() {
    i64 k = 10;
    Op outer = new Op((i64 x) use (k) => {
        Op inner = new Op((i64 y) use (k) => y + k);
        return inner(x) + k;
    });
    if (outer(1) != 21) return 1;                   // inner(1)=1+10=11, +k=10 -> 21
    return 0;
}

i64 manycap_check() {
    i64 acc = 0;
    i64 c1 = 1;
    i64 c2 = 2;
    i64 c3 = 3;
    i64 c4 = 4;
    i64 c5 = 5;
    i64 c6 = 6;
    i64 c7 = 7;
    i64 c8 = 8;
    i64 c9 = 9;
    i64 c10 = 10;
    i64 c11 = 11;
    i64 c12 = 12;
    i64 c13 = 13;
    i64 c14 = 14;
    Op f = new Op((i64 x) use (&acc, c1, c2, c3, c4, c5, c6, c7, c8, c9, c10, c11, c12, c13, c14) => {
        acc = acc + x + c1 + c2 + c3 + c4 + c5 + c6 + c7 + c8 + c9 + c10 + c11 + c12 + c13 + c14;
        return acc;
    });
    if (f(5) != 110) return 1;                     // c1..c14 sum to 105
    if (f(1) != 216) return 2;                     // the by-reference capture kept the first sum
    if (acc != 216) return 3;
    return 0;
}

i64 midbody_gen_check() {
    Op made = new Op(add1);                        // a thunk, BEFORE the closure (K6)
    i64[] xs = new i64[2];                         // ...and `new T[n]`'s own three
    Cell<i64> c = new Cell<i64>;                   // ...and a generic instance
    i64 acc = 0;
    Op byref = new Op((i64 x) use (&acc) => { acc = acc + x; return acc; });
    xs[0] = byref(3);
    c.v = byref(4);
    if (xs[0] != 3) return 1;
    if (c.v != 7) return 2;
    if (acc != 7) return 3;
    if (made(41) != 42) return 4;                  // the thunk still answers
    return 0;
}

class Gauge {
    i64 store;

    public i64 Side {
        get => store;
        set => store = value;
    }
}

i64 accessor_owner_check() {
    Gauge g = new Gauge();
    g.Side = 5;
    if (g.Side != 5) return 1;
    return 0;
}

// D70: `armGlobal` names only `d70_glob`, a global no member of `D70Member`
// shares the name of -- unchanged, the same global a plain read already
// gave. `armStatic` names a STATIC field and a STATIC method of its own
// class; `armConstProp` names a member CONST and a static PROPERTY -- none
// of the three needs a `this` a lambda never captures implicitly (D11), so
// all three still resolve, exactly as they do for the method itself, and
// every one of them wins over the identically spelled GLOBAL declared just
// above the class. `sarmDeleg`'s own STATIC delegate field is the fourth
// case, `member_deleg_check` below -- kept apart because the field itself
// outlives this function's own scope (`slot_roads_check`'s own floor).
i64 member_check() {
    D70Member.sfield = 5;
    D70Member.SProp = 6;
    D70Member m = new D70Member;
    m.armGlobal();
    if (m.cb(1) != 10) return 1;                   // 1 + d70_glob(9)
    m.armStatic();
    if (m.cb(1) != 8) return 2;                    // 1 + sfield(5) + stwice(1)=2
    m.armConstProp();
    if (m.cb(1) != 11) return 3;                   // 1 + SCONST(4) + SProp(6), not the globals (1+222+333)
    return 0;
}

i64 partial_close_check() {
    Shape s = new Shape();                         // the partial class closes HERE (K6)
    s.w = 3;
    s.h = 4;
    i64 acc = 0;
    Op byref = new Op((i64 x) use (&acc) => { acc = acc + x; return acc; });
    if (s.area() != 12) return 1;
    if (s.tag() != 7) return 2;                    // its interface table, emitted at the close too
    if (byref(5) != 5) return 3;
    if (acc != 5) return 4;
    return 0;
}

// D66: the two slots `Holder` above does not have -- a STATIC field and a
// field a CONSTRUCTOR writes through `this.` -- so `slot_roads_check` below
// covers every road one helper can reach.
class St {
    public static Op cb;
    public static i64 n;
}

class Ctor {
    public Op cb;
    public i64 n;

    public Ctor(i64 k) {
        i64 step = k;                        // `use` captures a local, not a parameter
        this.cb = (i64 x) use (step) => x + step;              // D66: the `this.` road
    }
}

i64 slot_roads_check() {
    Holder h = new Holder;
    h.cb = (i64 x) => x + 1;                                   // the FIELD road
    if (h.cb(41) != 42) return 1;
    h.cb = x => x * 2;                                         // ...its short grafia too
    if (h.cb(21) != 42) return 2;
    i64 k = 3;
    h.cb = (i64 x) use (k) => x * k;                           // ...and a capture by value
    if (h.cb(14) != 42) return 3;

    St.cb = (i64 x) => x + 2;                                  // the STATIC field road
    Op s = St.cb;
    if (s(40) != 42) return 4;

    Ctor c = new Ctor(2);                                      // the CONSTRUCTOR road
    if (c.cb(40) != 42) return 5;

    Op[] fs = new Op[2];                                       // the ELEMENT road
    fs[0] = (i64 x) => x * 2;
    fs[1] = x => x - 1;
    if (fs[0](21) != 42) return 6;
    if (fs[1](43) != 42) return 7;

    // ...and the same three roads still read a CAST and a GROUP exactly as
    // the core always read them: the lookahead is non-consuming and fires
    // only where the balanced `(...)` is followed by `=>` or `use`.
    c.n = (i64) 3.5;
    if (c.n != 3) return 8;
    c.n = (k + 1) * 2;
    if (c.n != 8) return 9;
    St.n = (i64) 2.9;
    if (St.n != 2) return 10;
    St.n = (k + 4) * 3;
    if (St.n != 21) return 11;
    fs[0] = (fs[1]);
    if (fs[0](43) != 42) return 12;

    return 0;
}

// D70: `D70Member.scb` (declared above, alongside `St`'s own static field)
// is a STATIC delegate field a STATIC method's own lambda calls bare --
// `sarmDeleg` reads `scb` the same way `armStatic` above reads `sfield`,
// with no `this` a lambda never captures implicitly (D11). Its own slot
// outlives this function's scope exactly as `St.cb` does, so this check
// runs beside `slot_roads_check`, not `member_check`, and adds one more to
// the floor `rt_live()` never drops back under.
i64 member_deleg_check() {
    D70Member.scb = (i64 x) => x * 5;
    Op sc = D70Member.sarmDeleg();
    if (sc(1) != 6) return 1;                      // 1 + scb(1)=5, the member's own target
    return 0;
}

// D66 (Copilot on #719): the three shapes of METHOD ARGUMENT the reader used
// to miss. `keep` STORES its `Op?` and never calls it -- calling through a
// nullable delegate is not taught (docs/reference/not-yet.md), and this row
// proves the PARSE of the argument, nothing more.
class ArgBase {
    public i64 inherited(Op f) {
        return f(20);
    }
}

class Args : ArgBase {
    public i64 keep(Op? f, i64 k) {
        Op? held = f;
        if (held == null) return 0;
        return k;
    }

    public i64 pick(Op f) {
        return f(1);
    }

    public i64 pick(Op f, i64 k) {
        return f(k);
    }
}

i64 arg_roads_check() {
    Args a = new Args;
    if (a.keep((i64 x) => x, 42) != 42) return 1;              // an `Op?` PARAMETER
    if (a.pick((i64 x) => x * 2, 21) != 42) return 2;          // an OVERLOADED name...
    if (a.pick(x => x + 41) != 42) return 3;                   // ...at the other arity
    if (a.inherited((i64 x) => x + 22) != 42) return 4;        // a method of the BASE

    // ...and the same reader leaves a GROUP at a delegate argument and a CAST
    // at the position beside it exactly where the core always read them.
    Op t = (i64 x) => x * 2;
    if (a.pick((t), 21) != 42) return 5;
    if (a.pick(t, (i64) 21.5) != 42) return 6;
    return 0;
}

i64 main() {
    i64 bad = nocap_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 10 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 20;

    bad = byval_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 30 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 40;

    bad = byref_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 50 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 60;

    bad = two_lambdas_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 70 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 80;

    bad = local_named_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 90 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 100;

    bad = method_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 110 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 120;

    bad = counted_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 130 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 140;

    if (geo.use_lambda() != 15) return 150;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 160;

    bad = block_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 170 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 180;

    bad = free_arg_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 190 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 200;

    bad = deleg_byval_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 210 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 220;

    bad = contextual_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 230 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 240;

    bad = short_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 250 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 260;

    bad = clean_f_returns_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 270 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 280;

    bad = ternary_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 290 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 300;

    bad = global_const_free_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 310 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 320;

    bad = nested_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 330 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 340;

    bad = manycap_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 350 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 360;

    bad = midbody_gen_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 370 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 380;

    bad = partial_close_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 390 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 400;

    bad = accessor_owner_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 410 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 420;

    bad = member_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 421 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 427;

    bad = arg_roads_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 430 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 0) return 440;

    // `St.cb` is a STATIC, so the closure it holds outlives every scope in
    // the program and is still counted here.
    bad = slot_roads_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 450 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 1) return 460;

    // LAST, and the one helper whose floor is not zero either: `D70Member.scb`
    // is a SECOND static field of delegate type, on top of `St.cb` above.
    // Nothing runs after it.
    bad = member_deleg_check();
    if (bad != 0) return 470 + bad;
    if (rt_live() != 2) return 480;

    return 42;
}
